          explanation: 'The most remarkable line of the Matsya episode — the tiny fish says to Manu: "I will be for your protection and you will be for mine." This mutual protection pact between the human and the divine is unique in Puranic literature. It establishes the relationship not as one of petitioner and grant-giver but as genuine mutuality: the human protects and nurtures the divine, and the divine protects and nurtures the human. The covenant is bilateral. Spirituality is not a one-way transaction.',
