          science: 'Research on charitable giving and wellbeing (Dunn, Norton, Aknin): giving to others is one of the most robustly documented sources of psychological wellbeing across cultures and income levels. It activates reward pathways, reduces stress hormones, and builds social connection. The Matsya Purana\'s prescription of dana as the Kali Yuga practice is precisely what the science of wellbeing recommends as the highest-return investment for happiness in a complex, fast-moving age.',
