          translation: 'In Satya Yuga, austerity (tapas) is primary; in Treta Yuga, knowledge (jnana) is declared; in Dvapara Yuga, sacrifice (yajna) is prescribed; in Kali Yuga, the foundation is giving (dana).',
          hindi: 'सत्ययुग में तप मुख्य है; त्रेतायुग में ज्ञान कहा गया है; द्वापरयुग में यज्ञ कहा गया है; कलियुग में दान की स्थिति है।',
          explanation: 'The Matsya Purana assigns a primary spiritual practice to each Yuga — and the descending sequence is not arbitrary. In Satya Yuga, when human lifespans are vast and inner capacity is full, the difficult path of austerity (tapas) is feasible. As each Yuga shortens and capacity diminishes, the path simplifies. Kali Yuga — our current age — is the Yuga of dana: simple giving. The message is radical hope for the present: you do not need to be a Satya Yuga sage or a Treta Yuga scholar. In Kali Yuga, the path is giving — your time, your resources, your attention, your presence.',
