          explanation: 'When they became disappointed, they sought means to get rid of their distress. As a consequence, they began to find faults with worldly things. Ont of this fault finding, true knowledge arose. Of the wise Munis in the Svayambhuva Manvantara, some turned out in the DvApaiayuga as the opponents of the Vedas. Then Ayurveda (medicine), astronomy and the other limbs of the Vedas, political economy, logic, metaphysics, the ceremonies of the Kalpa iiitras, the glosses, the Srnritis, and various other Astras became filled with doubts. No effort was crowned with success, unless the whole body, mind and deed were set to work. — 20-24.',
