          translation: 'Var&ftgl said: — ** The terrible Indra has caused me consteruation. He has beaten me and subjected me to great privations and feeling myself unequal to bear them, I have now mshed to put an end to my life. Lord! now grant me a son who may drive away all my sufferings." — 1-2. Hearing all that, the Daitya was surcharged with wrath and his eyes became bloodaliot with anger. Inspite of his being able to take ven- geance on Indra, he, however, decided to practise austerities when Brahma appeared before him, knowing his fierce intentions and addressed him with the following sweet words. — 3-5.',
